# Edge security headers (security audit 2026-08-20). Vite copies this file
# verbatim into dist/. It is the Netlify / Cloudflare Pages convention and is
# inert on hosts that don't read it — for nginx/Apache set the equivalents by
# hand (documented in docs/security-audit-2026-08-20.md).
#
# These cover the header-ONLY directives a meta CSP cannot express
# (frame-ancestors, X-Frame-Options, nosniff, Permissions-Policy). The full
# Content-Security-Policy is still shipped as a <meta> in index.html so the
# baseline applies on any host, header support or not.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(self), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
